# Open-Meteo
The weather to come, hour by hour, today and tomorrow, for a few cities.
Every thing it shows is in OpenMeteo.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
with `<spell-more-of>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
Open-Meteo has no list of forecasts:  each is asked for by a latitude and a longitude, so the page always says both.

<spell-thing "open meteo page">
	<spell>
		- its "cities" is a list of cities
		- its "city" is a city
		- to create it:
			add a new city with name = "Berlin", latitude = 52.52, longitude = 13.41 to its cities
			add a new city with name = "New York", latitude = 40.71, longitude = -74.01 to its cities
			add a new city with name = "Tokyo", latitude = 35.68, longitude = 139.69 to its cities
			add a new city with name = "Buenos Aires", latitude = -34.6, longitude = -58.38 to its cities
			set its city to the first item of its cities
	</spell>
	<property "forecasts" description="The city's, from Open-Meteo:  asked for by where it is, with no list of them all">every forecast where its latitude is the latitude of the city and its longitude is the longitude of the city</property>
	<property "forecast" description="Its one forecast:  Open-Meteo answers with one, for the nearest place it has">the first item of its forecasts</property>

	<draw>
		<header size="large">The weather, from Open-Meteo</header>
		<toolbar class="cities" appearance="secondary" aria-label="Cities">
			{draw each city in its cities}
		</toolbar>
		draw its hours
		<text class="credits" size="small">
			From <link link="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs">Open-Meteo's API</link>, asked for as you look;  each measure in your own units.
		</text>
	</draw>

	<draw "hours">
		<if its forecast>
			<text color="grey">The next two days in {the timezone of its forecast}, hour by hour.</text>
			<table class="hours" appearance="very-basic" unstackable>
				{draw each hour in the hours of its forecast}
			</table>
		</if>
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Asking Open-Meteo</loader>
		if that fails:
			<text>Open-Meteo can't be reached just now.</text>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# A city
Where it is on Earth:  what its forecast is asked for by.

<spell-thing "city">
	<spell>
		- its "name" is text
		- its "latitude" is a number
		- its "longitude" is a number
	</spell>

	<draw>
		<item active={it is the city of the weather of the public servers} onClick={pick it}>{its name}</item>
	</draw>
</spell-thing>


# An hour
Its day and hour, and each measure:  in the units the reader's region reads, °F and inches in the US.

<spell-more-of "hour">
	<draw>
		<row>
			<cell header>{its time} · {the hour of its time}:00</cell>
			<cell>{its temperature}</cell>
			<cell>{its precipitation}</cell>
			<cell>{its wind speed}</cell>
		</row>
	</draw>
</spell-more-of>
